# The same policy as ../input.lg with its declarations reordered: the human
# before the actor, the reservation before the gates it keys on, the gates
# swapped, and both groups of cords reversed. Declarations are
# order-independent in meaning (SYNTAX §3), so this denotes the same policy;
# determinism-repeat-permute requires the same activations run against this
# file to yield the same per-gate verdicts, master decisions and log trace
# as against ../input.lg.
human  alice  role legal
reserve automated_decision by legal when risk >= high
actor  bot7
gate   decide  risk high   grant bot7
gate   draft   risk low    grant bot7
cord decide -> master
cord draft  -> master
cord bot7   -> decide
cord bot7   -> draft
